# rlxfw's kernel configuration, expressed as a line-by-line delta with a reason
# per line.  R3-4.   Checked by: tools/kconfig-delta.py check
#
# baseline-drop: src-vendor/rtl819x-toolchain @ 5c9be5d9
# baseline-file: boards/rtl8196e/config.linux-2.6.30.RTL8196E_88E_GW
# baseline-sha256: 44f781de0cfd2ea9e59f7e9e4e01514976c1f3ef82e423f315fc955f558a862c
# baseline-bytes: 26548
# oldconfig-invocation: make -C linux-2.6.30 oldconfig < /dev/null
#
# WHICH DROP, AND WHY THE FILE NAME IS NOT ENOUGH.  Three of the four GPL drops
# on hand carry a file with this exact path.  量 2026-08-28: the two Actiontec
# ones are byte-identical to each other (26,414 bytes, md5 d37bbebd...) and
# DIFFER FROM THIS ONE on eight symbol lines -- CONFIG_RTL_ODM_WLAN_DRIVER,
# CONFIG_RTL_ETH_PRIV_SKB_DEBUG and CONFIG_RTL_EEE_DISABLED among them.  A
# baseline named by filename alone would be three different files.  The sha256
# above is the baseline; nothing else is.
#
# HOW THE 35 LINES BELOW WERE CLASSIFIED, AND WHY IT IS A MEASUREMENT.
# Every `derive` line claims kconfig produces that transition from the baseline
# with no input from me.  That claim was tested rather than asserted: a .config
# was built that ARGUES with all 21 of them at once -- asserting `=y` for the
# eighteen kconfig drops, `is not set` for the two it adds, and keeping the
# vendor's `is not set` for ARCH_CPU_SLEEP -- and `oldconfig` was run on it.
# 量: the output was identical on all 21.  The negative control is in the same
# file and is what makes that mean anything: CONFIG_SWAP was flipped in the
# same way and DID come back changed.  A run where nothing moved and nothing
# could have moved would have printed the same thing.
#
# WHY THERE ARE NO `(NEW)` PROMPTS LEFT, WHICH IS THE REAL ANSWER TO
# `yes '' | make oldconfig`.  On the vendor's template `oldconfig` is asked
# nothing at all -- `(NEW)` appears 0 times, and `< /dev/null`, `yes '' |`,
# `yes n |` and `yes y |` produce .config files with 0 differing symbol lines
# (量).  The banned string was inert.  It stopped being inert the moment rlxfw
# set CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y, which made a menu reachable and produced FOUR
# `(NEW)` prompts.  Rather than rely on how stdin is connected, every symbol
# that menu offers is written into the input .config below, so `(NEW)` is 0
# again and no answer -- empty, n, y or EOF -- can change the result.  The
# eleven such lines are marked `set`, because accepting a default is a choice
# and this file is where choices are written down.
#
# kind	symbol	from	to	mechanism	reason

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rlxfw's own changes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set	CONFIG_CMDLINE	"console=ttyS0,38400 root=/dev/mtdblock1"	"console=ttyS0,38400"	-	root= is removed. 讀 init/main.c:885-891: with an accessible /init the kernel never calls prepare_namespace(), so on a SUCCESSFUL initramfs boot this string is inert -- the reason to remove it is the failing boot. If the initramfs does not unpack, prepare_namespace() runs and mounts /dev/mtdblock1, which on this device is the vendor's own flash rootfs. That is a boot that would look like a pass, which is exactly the anti-DoD PROGRESS.md records. It costs nothing and it also makes the `Kernel command line:` line a discriminator, since the vendor's carries root= and mine does not
set	CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD	n	y	-	Decision B (notes/kernel-build.md 4): the first boot mounts an initramfs built from this unit's own userspace rather than the flash rootfs. Without this the initramfs is not linked in at all and the kernel falls through to root=
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE	-	"usr/rlxfw-initramfs.spec"	-	the gen_init_cpio spec tools/mkinitramfs.py emits from config/rlxfw-initramfs.tsv. Relative to the kernel directory on purpose: an absolute path would tie the build to one scratch directory. usr/Makefile:31 falls back to `-d` -- an image holding one empty directory -- if the file is missing, so tools/rlxfw-kbuild.sh checks the path rather than trusting it
set	CONFIG_MTD_CHAR	n	y	-	the kernel-enforced read-only path to flash, and it is the whole reason this rebuild happened. 讀 drivers/mtd/mtdchar.c mtd_open: `if ((file->f_mode & FMODE_WRITE) && (minor & 1)) return -EACCES` -- an ODD minor cannot be opened for writing BY THE KERNEL, which is stronger than any mode bit because root ignores DAC. With this set, /dev/mtd0ro (c 90 1; 讀 include/linux/mtd/mtd.h:21 `#define MTD_CHAR_MAJOR 90`) is a read of mtd0 -- the partition holding the loader and H601 -- that CANNOT write it. PREDICTION, written before the build: (NEW) stays 0. 讀 drivers/mtd/Kconfig:175, tristate with no `depends on` of its own; 量 over the whole drop, `depends on MTD_CHAR` and `select MTD_CHAR` return ZERO hits, and drivers/mtd/Makefile:18 `obj-$(CONFIG_MTD_CHAR) += mtdchar.o` is the symbol's only consumer -- so nothing new becomes reachable, which is what section 6.6's trap is about. REFUTED BY any (NEW) line in the oldconfig log, in which case the symbol it names gets pinned here the way CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME did. ⚠️ mtdchar.c is byte-identical across the three GPL drops that carry it (量 2026-08-30, md5 83d6fc7bbec987be1cbca27d8bc006bd), so the enforcement is ONE SOURCE IN THREE COPIES and stays 讀 until `echo x > /dev/mtd0ro` returns EACCES on the silicon
set	CONFIG_GPIOLIB	-	y	-	R5-4, 2026-09-06. rtl819x-gpio registers a struct gpio_chip, so gpiolib has to be in the image. It is NOT reachable on this arch without config/host-compat/0005: 量 cell r54gate, this line alone appended to the ea6ee537 .config and oldconfig DROPPED it, while the positive control in the same run (CONFIG_SWAP flipped to y) survived. With 0005 applied the same input keeps it (cell r54gate2). obj-y and not obj-$(CONFIG_...) links rtl819x-gpio.o unconditionally (MK3), so removing THIS line does not silently ship an image without the driver -- it fails to link on gpiochip_add, which is the loud failure and is why the Makefile row is written that way
set	CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256	n	y	-	R5-5, 2026-09-07.  rtl819x-spi computes a sha256 over H601's complement INSIDE this kernel, so crypto/sha256_generic.c has to be in the image.  讀 crypto/Kconfig:368, tristate with `select CRYPTO_HASH`, and CONFIG_CRYPTO_HASH=y / CRYPTO_HASH2=y are already in the baseline, so nothing new becomes reachable and PREDICTION, written before the build: (NEW) stays 0.  量 crypto/Makefile:45 `obj-$(CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256) += sha256_generic.o` is the symbol's only consumer, and :27-28 build shash.o under CRYPTO_HASH2, so crypto_alloc_shash links.  🔴 THE REASON THIS NEEDS A KAT AND NOT JUST A SYMBOL: CONFIG_CRYPTO_MANAGER is `is not set` in the baseline, so the crypto core runs NO self-test on registration -- 讀 crypto/algapi.c crypto_wait_for_test(), where with no notifier to consume it crypto_probing_notify returns NOTIFY_DONE and crypto_alg_tested() is called directly, completing the larval WITHOUT testing anything.  That same branch is why crypto_alloc_shash works here at all.  REFUTED BY: crypto_alloc_shash returning an error (the driver's S4 mark prints it), or a boot that stalls inside crypto_wait_for_test's wait_for_completion, in which case this line comes out and the driver carries its own sha256.  The driver's three FIPS 180-2 vectors are the positive control that the engine works on this die, and the 56-byte one is there because it crosses the 55-byte padding boundary

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pinned so that oldconfig has nothing to ask.  Each value is what kconfig
# computes; writing it here is what makes the build independent of stdin.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_ROOT_UID	-	0	-	the image is built as root-owned; gen_init_cpio takes uid 0 from the spec's own columns as well, and these two must agree
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_ROOT_GID	-	0	-	as above
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_NONE	-	y	-	the cpio goes into .init.data uncompressed. 579,644 bytes of content against 2,395,932 bytes of headroom under the 5,242,880 ceiling (notes/kernel-build.md 3.4), so compression buys margin this gate does not need and adds a decompressor to rung 1's critical path. This is kconfig's default; it is written down because a default that changes silently is the thing this file exists to catch
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_GZIP	-	n	-	the other three arms of the same choice, pinned with it
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_BZIP2	-	n	-	as above
set	CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_LZMA	-	n	-	as above
set	CONFIG_RD_GZIP	-	y	-	kconfig's default. It does not compress THIS image (COMPRESSION_NONE above); it is the kernel's ability to unpack a gzipped initrd handed to it by something else, and it costs DECOMPRESS_GZIP
set	CONFIG_RD_BZIP2	-	n	-	not needed and not free
set	CONFIG_RD_LZMA	-	n	-	not needed. Note the loader's own kernel wrapper is LZMA (notes/kernel-build.md 3.2); that decompressor is in rtkload and is a different program from this one
set	CONFIG_DECOMPRESS_GZIP	-	y	-	lib/decompress_inflate.c, pulled in by RD_GZIP above. Not independently settable; pinned so the line does not appear as an undeclared difference
set	CONFIG_PROBE_INITRD_HEADER	-	n	-	kconfig's default. It makes the kernel sniff an initrd header out of memory the bootloader left behind, and this gate hands the kernel nothing that way -- the image is entered at 0x80500000 by `J` with no initrd argument

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived by kconfig from the baseline, with no input from me.  All 21 were
# argued with at once and none moved; CONFIG_SWAP, argued with in the same
# file, did.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- promptless: the value is the default and no .config line reaches it ------
derive	CONFIG_ARCH_CPU_SLEEP	n	y	promptless	boards/rtl8196e/config.in:30 declares it `bool` with NO prompt string and `default y`, so sym_is_changable() is false and the vendor's own `# ... is not set` in the template is a dead line. 量: it comes out y under `< /dev/null`, `yes ''`, `yes n` AND `yes y`. 🔴 And it is not a defect to fix: the sleep instruction 0x42000038 is at 0x80007EA8 in THIS UNIT'S OWN SHIPPED KERNEL and at the matching place in mine, both in cpu_idle via arch/rlx/kernel/process.c:55. The vendor ships it on. The same symbol is `default n` under boards/rtl8198, so the value is board-specific and deliberate
derive	CONFIG_CPU_HAS_SLEEP	-	y	promptless	arch/rlx/Kconfig:83, `bool` with no prompt and `default y if ARCH_CPU_SLEEP`. It is what actually reaches the code: arch/rlx/include/asm/processor.h:31 makes __cpu_wait() emit `sleep` under it

# -- selected by another symbol, so it cannot be lowered ----------------------
derive	CONFIG_RTL_ODM_WLAN_DRIVER	-	y	selected	drivers/net/wireless/rtl8192cd/Kconfig:15 `select`s it, so kconfig forces y and never offers the prompt its own declaration at line 171 carries. ⚠️ It is ABSENT from this drop's template while the two Actiontec drops both carry `CONFIG_RTL_ODM_WLAN_DRIVER=y` -- the line was blanked in this copy, which is one of the eight ways the three templates differ
derive	CONFIG_ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB	-	y	selected	config/host-compat/0005 adds `select ARCH_WANT_OPTIONAL_GPIOLIB` to arch/rlx/Kconfig's `config MIPS`, so kconfig writes it out. 量 cell r54gate3 (patch applied, NO gpio line in the input): the whole diff against the input is four lines -- the datestamp, this symbol, and `# CONFIG_GPIOLIB is not set`. It gates nothing that is built: 量 over the staged tree it appears in 0 Makefile/Kbuild files and 0 .c/.h files, with the same two greps for CONFIG_GPIOLIB returning 1 and 10 as the positive control
derive	CONFIG_GENERIC_GPIO	-	y	selected	drivers/gpio/Kconfig:31 -- `menuconfig GPIOLIB` carries `select GENERIC_GPIO`, so asking for GPIOLIB forces it. It cannot be asked for directly: arch/rlx/Kconfig:275 declares it `bool` with no prompt, and 量 cell r54gate showed a CONFIG_GENERIC_GPIO=y in the input dropped for that reason. It is what R5-7 (LEDS_GPIO) and R5-8 (KEYBOARD_GPIO) both depend on

# -- the prompt's `depends on` is not satisfied by this model -----------------
# This unit IS the 88E model (CONFIG_RTL_88E_SUPPORT=y), so every symbol that
# says `depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT` is unreachable.  Ten of them.
derive	CONFIG_ANT_SWITCH	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:33, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_ENABLE_EFUSE	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:114, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_HIGH_POWER_EXT_PA	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:23, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_MP_PSD_SUPPORT	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:138, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_RTL_92D_SUPPORT	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:43, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_RTL_DUAL_PCIESLOT_BIWLAN_D	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:73, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_RTL_MESH_SUPPORT	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:161, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_RTL_P2P_SUPPORT	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:143, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_RTL_WAPI_SUPPORT	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:118, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_RTL_WLAN_DOS_FILTER	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:166, depends on RTL8192CD && !RTL_88E_SUPPORT
derive	CONFIG_HIGH_POWER_EXT_LNA	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:28, depends on RTL8192CD && RTL_92C_SUPPORT -- and RTL_92C_SUPPORT is absent from the built .config entirely
derive	CONFIG_RTL_HOSTAPD_SUPPORT	n	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:18, depends on RTL8192CD && RTL_92C_SUPPORT. It is also declared promptless in five boards' config.in, this board's included, which is why it is dropped rather than written out as n
derive	CONFIG_PHY_EAT_40MHZ	y	-	dep-unmet	rtl8192cd/Kconfig:151, depends on !AUTO_PCIE_PHY_SCAN, and CONFIG_AUTO_PCIE_PHY_SCAN=y in the built .config. ⚠️ This is the one derived line whose baseline value is y rather than n, so it is the one where "kconfig dropped it" and "something turned it off" look most alike from a diff. It is a drop: the symbol is absent, not set to n

# -- no `config` block declares it anywhere the board can reach ---------------
derive	CONFIG_PCIE_POWER_SAVING	n	-	undeclared	no `config` declaration anywhere under the drop. A line in the template for a symbol kconfig has never heard of
derive	CONFIG_RTL8190	n	-	undeclared	as above
derive	CONFIG_RTL8192SE	n	-	undeclared	as above
derive	CONFIG_RTL_8196E_ULINKER	n	-	undeclared	as above. Note the similarly named CONFIG_RTL_ULINKER below IS declared, under a different board
derive	CONFIG_RTL_ULINKER	n	-	other-board	declared only in boards/rtl8196eu/config.in:186. arch/rlx/Kconfig:10 sources ../target/config.in and `target` is a symlink to boards/rtl8196e, so this board never sees it

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE `loud` VARIANT.  R3-6, 2026-08-28.
#
# A row whose kind carries `@loud` is in the loud image only; a row with no
# variant is in both.  ONE file, two images -- a second delta would be a copy
# of the 35 rules above and a copy is a second owner.
#
# WHY THERE ARE TWO IMAGES AT ALL.  With the vendor's configuration this board
# prints NOTHING between kernel entry and userspace: printk is a stub,
# early_printk is a weak empty stub, and this unit's own capture
# (bench/2026-08-24c/G6.log) goes from `start address:` straight to the WLAN
# driver.  `quiet` keeps that -- it is what the vendor ships and it is the
# image whose behaviour is closest to the one thing known to boot on this
# silicon.  `loud` turns printk on and is the one the first seating uploads.
# If loud reaches D5 and quiet does not, that difference is a FINDING about
# the vendor's configuration and is recorded, not averaged.
#
# COST, measured rather than estimated: decompressed image 3,472,384 ->
# 3,546,112 (+73,728, +2.1 %), margin 1,770,496 -> 1,696,768, 66.2 % -> 67.6 %
# of the 5,242,880 ceiling.  hazlint P1 on the loud image: 0 violations in
# 111,801 loads.  The estimate written before the build was "150-300 KB" and
# it was wrong by 2-4x, which is what an uncalibrated guess is worth here.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set@loud	CONFIG_PRINTK	n	y	-	the kernel's own diagnostics: Memory:, Kernel command line, driver messages and panic backtraces. 讀 init/Kconfig:834, CONFIG_PRINTK is `default n` with a prompt gated on EMBEDDED and `depends on (!RTL_819X) || (RTL_819X && PRINTK_FUNC)`. 量 on the built config: EMBEDDED=y and PRINTK_FUNC=y, so it HAS a prompt and is settable -- checked before it was written here, because CONFIG_ARCH_CPU_SLEEP was the same shape and was NOT settable and R3-4 spent a session on that. What this does not buy: it reaches nothing before init/main.c:629 console_init(), which is why six of the eleven boot marks exist
set@loud	CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME	-	y	-	pinned so oldconfig has nothing to ask -- 量, setting PRINTK alone takes (NEW) from 0 to 1 and this is the symbol it asks about, which is section 6.6's trap firing on the first attempt. The VALUE is y and that is a measurement, not a default: printk_time reads cpu_clock -> sched_clock, and arch/rlx defines NO sched_clock (讀, zero hits), so the weak generic at kernel/sched_clock.c:39 is used -- (jiffies - INITIAL_JIFFIES) * (NSEC_PER_SEC / HZ) with CONFIG_HZ=100. It is NOT the CP0 Count register, which would have made every line read 0.000000 on this die (F50b, 量 2026-08-25b: Count is not implemented). So timestamps are real at 10 ms, and the transition from 0.000000 to a moving value marks where the timer interrupt started -- an observable the ladder gets free. REFUTED BY: every line reading 0.000000 through to userspace, which would be a finding about time_init and not about printk

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R5-6, 2026-09-08.  Four rows, and the first one is the gate's decision.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set	CONFIG_RTL_WTDOG	y	n	-	R5-6, 2026-09-08. THE VENDOR ARMS THE WATCHDOG AT OVSEL 3 AND FEEDS IT AT 100 Hz, AND BOTH HALVES ARE UNDER THIS SYMBOL. 讀 boards/rtl8196e/bsp/timer.c:82 `REG32(BSP_WDTCNR) = 0x00600000` = OVSEL 3 = 2^18 ticks = 1,334.723 ms 量 seating 17 (this row said 17.517 ms until 2026-09-09; that figure used CLK-08b's LOADER-state 14.965 MHz and is wrong by 76x -- the decision is unchanged, because an unconditional 100 Hz kick defeats a watchdog at either deadline); 讀 arch/rlx/kernel/rlx-cevt.c:159 `WDTCNR |= 1<<23` in the tick handler. 量 on the artefact (cell spi11's vmlinux, 2026-09-08): nine instructions form 0xB800311C and they resolve through System.map to five owners -- bsp_timer_init+0xb8 (the arm), rlx_timer_interrupt +0x60 (the kick) and +0x4c (the is_fault reboot), bsp_machine_restart +0xb4, write_watchdog_reboot+0x84, and three kicks in the wlan driver. 🔴 A /dev/watchdog shipped beside a 100 Hz unconditional kick CANNOT BITE, which is CLAUDE.md's `a tool that cannot fail proves nothing` in driver form -- so this is not a tidy-up, it is the precondition for R5-6 existing. PREDICTION, written before the build: the nine fall to TWO plus rtl819x-wdt's own. The two survivors are bsp_machine_restart (boards/rtl8196e/bsp/setup.c:114) and write_watchdog_reboot (drivers/char/rtl_gpio.c:2178); neither is inside any #if, 讀, and they matter for opposite reasons -- the first is how `busybox reboot -f` resets this board at all (FW-37: 2.407 s to the loader prompt, which is what buys twelve boots per power press), the second is a vendor `bite now` instrument that survives as an independent control on the driver's own bite. The three wlan kicks go with this symbol because CONFIG_RTL865X_WTDOG, the other arm of every `#if defined(A) || defined(B)` around them, is ABSENT from autoconf.h (量). REFUTED BY: any third survivor in the disassembly, or `busybox reboot -f` failing to reset the board. WHAT IS GIVEN UP, written down rather than discovered later: kernel/panic.c:101 and kernel/exit.c:925 set is_fault under this symbol, so with it off a panic no longer reboots. 推, with the arithmetic: with it ON the next tick arrives within 10 ms and bites 2.19 ms later, and at 38400 8N1 that is ~46 characters -- a truncated panic, which is why this tree carries 97 panic_printk sites (FW-31). With it off a panic PRINTS, which is what a bring-up firmware wants. Refuted by a capture of a vendor-kernel panic longer than ~46 characters. The safety net that is also lost -- `the TC0 interrupt stopped` -- is replaced by rtl819x-wdt's BOOTGUARD state one layer up, which catches the timer wheel wedging as well.
set	CONFIG_WATCHDOG	n	y	-	R5-6, 2026-09-08. drivers/Makefile:79 is `obj-$(CONFIG_WATCHDOG) += watchdog/`, so without this the directory holding rtl819x-wdt.c is never descended into, MK6's Kbuild line is never read, and the build is GREEN with no driver in the image. That silent mode is why MK6's witness is a string against the built artefact. 讀 drivers/watchdog/Kconfig:5, `menuconfig WATCHDOG`, bool, no `depends on`, so it is settable -- checked before it was written here, because CONFIG_ARCH_CPU_SLEEP was the same shape and was NOT settable and R3-4 spent a session on that. PREDICTION, written before the build: exactly TWO symbols become reachable that were not. 量 by enumerating every `config` entry in that Kconfig and its `depends on`: WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT and SOFT_WATCHDOG are the only two with none, and both are pinned below, so `(NEW)` stays 0. REFUTED BY any (NEW) line in the oldconfig log, in which case the symbol it names gets pinned here the way CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME did. Nothing else in the directory is built: every other entry is obj-$(CONFIG_x) for a symbol this .config does not carry, and the MIPS block's five are all for other platforms.
set	CONFIG_WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT	-	n	-	R5-6, 2026-09-08. Pinned so oldconfig has nothing to ask. 讀 drivers/watchdog/Kconfig:31. The VALUE is n and it is a decision, not an accepted default: rtl819x-wdt implements nowayout as a module parameter, so honouring the compile-time symbol as well would make one policy have two owners -- house rule 1, in a driver. It is also the wrong default for this project: one device, no spare, and a watchdog that can never be released back to BOOTGUARD turns a wedged test daemon into a reboot loop that costs a power cycle to leave.
set	CONFIG_SOFT_WATCHDOG	-	n	-	R5-6, 2026-09-08. Pinned so oldconfig has nothing to ask. 讀 drivers/watchdog/Kconfig:48, tristate with no `depends on`, which is why turning CONFIG_WATCHDOG on makes it reachable at all. 🔴 The VALUE is n for a reason that is not size: softdog registers the SAME miscdevice minor rtl819x-wdt does -- WATCHDOG_MINOR 130, 讀 include/linux/miscdevice.h:15 -- so with both built in, whichever registers second takes -EBUSY from misc_register and the image ships a /dev/watchdog whose identity depends on link order. rtl819x-wdt reports misc_rc in /proc precisely so that collision would be a field rather than a mystery, but not having it is better than detecting it.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A CORRECTION, 2026-09-08.  Found by running the gate this file describes
# against three images that had already shipped.  The gate was right and
# nobody had run it; see the row's own reason.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set	CONFIG_GPIO_SYSFS	-	n	-	🔴 2026-09-08, and this row is a CORRECTION that R5-6's segment found rather than part of R5-6. 量: `kconfig-delta check` REFUSES on the built .config of r54b, r55b AND spi11 with `UNDECLARED: CONFIG_GPIO_SYSFS - -> n`, and each of those three oldconfig logs carries exactly one `(NEW)` line -- `/sys/class/gpio/... (sysfs interface) (GPIO_SYSFS) [N/y/?] (NEW)` -- while r53b2, the build immediately before R5-4, carries ZERO. So it entered with CONFIG_GPIOLIB=y on 2026-09-06 and has been undeclared in every image since, INCLUDING the one seating 16 ran. 讀 drivers/gpio/Kconfig:51, `bool "/sys/class/gpio/... (sysfs interface)"`, `depends on SYSFS && EXPERIMENTAL`, and 量 both are y in this .config -- so it is offered, every time. 🔴 THIS FILE'S OWN HEADER SAYS THE OPPOSITE AND HAS BEEN WRONG FOR TWO DAYS: `every symbol that menu offers is written into the input .config below, so `(NEW)` is 0 again and no answer -- empty, n, y or EOF -- can change the result`. That stopped being true the day GPIOLIB went in. Nothing caught it because kconfig-delta check is not run by rlxfw-kbuild.sh and has to be typed, which is the same shape as LOG.md's note that `rlxfw-marks verify` is never run automatically either. ⚠ THE THREE IMAGES ARE NOT WRONG: the value taken was n, which is what this row declares, so no shipped behaviour changes and no measurement is retracted. What was wrong is that the value was decided by HOW STDIN HAPPENED TO BE CONNECTED -- `--oldconfig yes` answers y to a `[N/y/?]` -- which is exactly the class of accident this file exists to close. THE VALUE is n on its merits too: R5-4's gpio_chip ships with ALLOW_OUT_MASK 0 and one known line, and a sysfs export path gives userspace a SECOND way into direction_output whose refusals are not the ones /proc/rtl819x-gpio counts -- two doors into one guard with only one of them instrumented. REFUTED BY a `(NEW)` line naming GPIO_SYSFS in any build after this row lands.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R5-7, 2026-09-10.  FIVE rows, and the count is the finding: the step was
# planned as three.
#
# THE PREDICTION, WRITTEN BEFORE THE BUILD, and it is an enumeration rather
# than a hope.  量 2026-09-10 by parsing drivers/leds/Kconfig against
# r57.config-built with NEW_LEDS/LEDS_CLASS/LEDS_GPIO forced on and every
# `if`, `depends on` and prompt evaluated: 35 symbols in that file, FIVE
# reachable prompts, and exactly TWO of the five absent from the .config --
# LEDS_GPIO_PLATFORM and LEDS_TRIGGERS.  Both are pinned below, so `(NEW)`
# stays 0.  REFUTED BY any (NEW) line in the oldconfig log, in which case the
# symbol it names gets pinned here the way CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME did.
#
# The other twenty-seven LEDS_* drivers are unreachable on their SECOND
# dependency -- I2C, X86, SPI, MFD_WM8350, ARCH_S3C2410, MIPS_COBALT and so on
# -- and LEDS_GPIO_OF on OF_DEVICE, which this arch does not have.  That is
# what makes the two a bounded list and not a sample.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set	CONFIG_NEW_LEDS	n	y	-	R5-7, 2026-09-10. drivers/Makefile:94 is `obj-$(CONFIG_NEW_LEDS) += leds/`, so without this the directory holding leds-gpio.c and led-class.c is never descended into and the build is GREEN with no LED support in the image -- the same silent mode CONFIG_WATCHDOG's row above was written for. 讀 drivers/leds/Kconfig:1, `menuconfig NEW_LEDS`, bool, no `depends on`, so it is settable; checked before it was written here, because CONFIG_ARCH_CPU_SLEEP was the same shape and was NOT settable and R3-4 spent a session on that. It is the one row of the five whose baseline is an explicit line rather than an absence: 量, the template carries `# CONFIG_NEW_LEDS is not set` at :857.
set	CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS	-	y	-	R5-7, 2026-09-10. The /sys/class/leds infrastructure leds-gpio registers into. 讀 drivers/leds/Kconfig:11, tristate, `if NEW_LEDS` and nothing else, so turning NEW_LEDS on makes it reachable and it must be answered here rather than by whatever stdin happens to be -- which is the accident CONFIG_GPIO_SYSFS's row above records. =y and not =m: this image has no module loader in its userspace and led_classdev_register is called at device_initcall.
set	CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO	-	y	-	R5-7, 2026-09-10. The upstream driver itself. 讀 drivers/leds/Kconfig:121, tristate, `depends on LEDS_CLASS && GENERIC_GPIO` -- and GENERIC_GPIO is already y and is derived rather than set (its row above records that GPIOLIB `select`s it and that it cannot be asked for directly). 🔴 R5-7 uses the UPSTREAM driver rather than one of mine, and that is the step's evidential claim rather than a shortcut: an unmodified upstream consumer binding to my gpio_chip is evidence a driver I wrote myself cannot produce, which is the same reason R5-4 routed its own claim/release verbs through gpiolib. notes/gpio-driver.md 9.
set	CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO_PLATFORM	-	y	-	R5-7, 2026-09-10. 🔴 THIS IS THE ROW THE STEP WAS PLANNED WITHOUT, and without it the other four ship an image in which nothing binds. 讀 drivers/leds/leds-gpio.c: gpio_led_probe, the platform_driver that carries it, and the platform_driver_register call inside gpio_led_init are ALL inside `#ifdef CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO_PLATFORM`. With it unset, leds-gpio compiles, links, and registers no platform driver at all, so arch/rlx/kernel/rlxfw-devices.c's platform_device sits on the bus for ever with no driver -- and with CONFIG_PRINTK=n there is not one message about it. 讀 drivers/leds/Kconfig:131, bool, `depends on LEDS_GPIO`, `default y`: it would have come out y on its own, and relying on that is exactly the implicit dependency this file exists to make explicit. 🟢 It is ALSO enforced at build time from the other side -- rlxfw-devices.c carries an #error on this symbol -- because CFG-2 records that `kconfig-delta check` is never invoked by rlxfw-kbuild.sh, so this file and the built .config can drift with nothing noticing.
set	CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGERS	-	n	-	R5-7, 2026-09-10. Pinned so oldconfig has nothing to ask. 讀 drivers/leds/Kconfig, bool, `depends on` nothing but the enclosing `if NEW_LEDS`, so it becomes reachable the moment NEW_LEDS goes y -- it is one of the two symbols the enumeration above predicts. THE VALUE is n on its merits, not only for size: a trigger is a second writer of the same LED on a timer, and PABCD bit 6 already HAS a second writer -- the vendor's rtl_gpio_timer blinks it (量 FW-40, REG-37). notes/gpio-driver.md 6 is the contention argument and its instrument is a foreign-write detector whose reading is `is anything other than me writing this bit`; adding a kernel timer of my own that also writes it would make that reading unattributable by construction. 🟢 It also keeps the count at two: its six children (LEDS_TRIGGER_TIMER, _IDE_DISK, _HEARTBEAT, _BACKLIGHT, _GPIO, _DEFAULT_ON) all `depends on LEDS_TRIGGERS`, so n leaves every one of them unreachable and `(NEW)` at 0.
